# Rust
#
# `/target` (anchored, no trailing slash) rather than `target/`: since
# 2026-07-29 the build dir is a SYMLINK to /Users/Shared/cargo-targets/mcp-methods
# on the internal disk, and a `dir/` pattern does not match a symlink — it
# showed up as untracked. Nested per-example targets are listed separately below.
/target
Cargo.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
wheels/
*.so
*.dylib
*.dSYM/
*.pyd
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Virtual environments
.venv*/
venv/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Secrets
.env

# OS
.DS_Store

# Inbox — local coordination mail with kglite / mcp-servers. See the
# "Mail interface" section in CLAUDE.md for the schema and counterparts.
inbox/

# Local dev working folder — the backlog index (todos.md) and its plans/
# detail docs, plus the `.doctrine-synced` marker the release skill's step 0
# reads and writes. Never committed: it carries in-flight intent and
# sibling-project paths, and this repo is public. It is also unbacked, so
# nothing committed may cite a path inside it as an instruction — a citation
# outlives the file and silently becomes a dangling pointer. Its size/file
# bound is `make check-dev-docs`, and the conventions it adopts or declines
# belong in CLAUDE.md or the commit that decided them.
#
# NOT the same thing as the tracked, public `dev-documentation/` folder, which
# holds durable design write-ups meant to be read by consumers of the crate.
/dev-docs/

# Workstation-local agent configuration and skills. The .claude/skills/
# authority and .agents/skills/ adapter remain on disk, outside the public
# repository. Shared procedures are maintained by the doctrine project;
# untracking a previously published skill does not remove its git history.
/.claude/
/.agents/

# Bundled mcp-server binary (built by `make bundle-bin` or the wheel CI step)
python/mcp_methods/_bin/
examples/downstream_binary/target/
examples/downstream_binary/Cargo.lock

# Sphinx build output (Read the Docs builds this itself; local previews only)
docs/_build/
